# all.aon --- the instance: one model, three units, one run.
#
# Each generator contributes a UNIT under `units` and the rule set that
# fills it; this document includes the three and lists their units as
# the aontu:code instance `aontu render` reads. One run renders the
# whole set, and `--out` writes nothing unless every unit rendered --
# which check.sh proves by breaking one. `--unit <path>` renders one of
# them alone.
#
# The generators are included at the root rather than as values, and
# their aliases carry the target's name (`%go_record`, `%ts_record`),
# because an alias declaration is a key of the document that includes
# it: two files declaring `%record` would meet, and a document included
# as a value cannot resolve its own aliases (use-cases/BUGS.md 85).
@"./gen-go.aon"
@"./gen-ts.aon"
@"./gen-sql.aon"

aontu: Code: units: [$.units.go $.units.ts $.units.sql]
